{"schema_version":"1.9.2","id":"DHI-kxbh-fwxk-qzly-g75w","published":"2026-11-19T06:15:58Z","modified":"2026-11-20T14:45:35.179851157Z","upstream":["CVE-2026-127231"],"summary":"A double free in the X.509 name constraints enforcement of GnuTLS 3.8.13 on all platforms allows a remote attacker to…","details":"A double free in the X.509 name constraints enforcement of GnuTLS 3.8.13 on all platforms allows a remote attacker to cause a denial of service (application crash) via a certificate chain containing a NameConstraints extension processed while the application is under memory pressure. When an already populated name constraints object is reinitialized, previously freed list pointers are not cleared, so a memory allocation failure precisely at reinitialization leaves a dangling pointer that is freed again during a later cleanup.","affected":[{"package":{"name":"gnutls","ecosystem":"Docker Hardened Images:Alpine:3.23","purl":"pkg:apk/dhi/gnutls"},"versions":["3.8.11-r0","3.8.12-r0","3.8.13-r0"],"database_specific":{"owner_kind":"HSP","source":"https://github.com/docker-hardened-images/advisories/blob/main/dhi/osv/2026/DHI-kxbh-fwxk-qzly-g75w.json"}},{"package":{"name":"gnutls","ecosystem":"Docker Hardened Images:Alpine:3.24","purl":"pkg:apk/dhi/gnutls"},"versions":["3.8.13-r0","3.8.14-r0"],"database_specific":{"owner_kind":"HSP","source":"https://github.com/docker-hardened-images/advisories/blob/main/dhi/osv/2026/DHI-kxbh-fwxk-qzly-g75w.json"}},{"package":{"name":"gnutls28","ecosystem":"Docker Hardened Images:Debian:13","purl":"pkg:deb/dhi/gnutls28"},"versions":["3.8.9-3+deb13u4+dhi2"],"database_specific":{"owner_kind":"HSP","source":"https://github.com/docker-hardened-images/advisories/blob/main/dhi/osv/2026/DHI-kxbh-fwxk-qzly-g75w.json"}}],"references":[{"type":"ADVISORY","url":"https://scout.docker.com/v/DHI-kxbh-fwxk-qzly-g75w"},{"type":"ADVISORY","url":"https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-127231"},{"type":"ADVISORY","url":"https://security.alpinelinux.org/